## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates how candidates design end-to-end data-fetch pipelines with planning, dynamic re-planning, and observability in a production analytics context.

## Key Concepts
- LangChain agent workflows and orchestration
- AutoGen planning, tool-use patterns, and multi-agent coordination
- Idempotent REST calls with cache coherence guarantees
- Dynamic re-planning on failures with rollback paths
- Observability: distributed tracing, latency metrics, and freshness validation

## Code Example
```javascript
function buildPlan(input) {
  const planner = new AutoGenPlanner({
    tools: [restTool, cacheTool, loggingTool],
    retryConfig: { maxAttempts: 3, backoffMultiplier: 2 },
    onFailure: 'replan'
  });
  return planner.createPlan({ input, phases: ['fetch', 'validate', 'cache'] });
}
```

Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates hands-on design of a real-time RAG system, including multi-embedding chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and data freshness in production-like conditions.

Key Concepts
- Dual-embedding chunking
- Vector DB indexing and cosine search
- Cross-encoder reranking
- Streaming updates and TTL pruning
- Latency targets and observability

Code Example
```javascript
async function retrieve(query) {
  const eSent = await embed(query, 'sentence');
  const eSect = await embed(query, 'section');
  const topSent = vectorDB.search(eSent,  topK);
  const topSect = vectorDB.search(eSect, topK);
  // fuse and rerank
  return rerank(topSent, topSect, query);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and improve retrieval quality in production?
- How would your design adapt if the vector DB spans multiple regions with different latencies?

## Why Asked
Tests understanding of RAG preprocessing and retrieval optimization

## Key Concepts
- Semantic chunking vs fixed-size splitting
- Sliding window overlap strategies
- Document structure awareness
- Embedding model context limitations

## Code Example
```
function chunkDocument(content, strategy) {
  switch(strategy) {
    case 'semantic':
      return splitBySentences(content)
        .groupIntoChunks(512)
        .withOverlap(50);
    case 'sliding':
      return createSlidingWindow(content, 300, 50);
  }
}
```

